        "abstract": "<jats:p>We investigate dynamic correlation functions for a pair of exchange-coupled classical spins with biaxial exchange and/or single-site anisotropy. This represents a Hamiltonian system with two degrees of freedom for which we have previously established the integrability criteria. We discuss the impact of (non-)integrability on the autocorrelation functions and their spectral properties. We point out the role of long-time anomalies caused by low-flux cantori, which dominate the convergence properties of time averages and determine the long-time asymptotic behavior of autocorrelation functions in nonintegrable cases.</jats:p>",
        "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.340524",
        "type": "journal-article"
